3:01:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50526154/south-carolina-qb-lanorris-sellers-set-play-vs-georgia","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NC State names NFL assistant Jason Michael as OC under Philip Rivers","published":"2026-11-19T12:21:56.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50524698/nc-state-names-nfl-assistant-michael-oc-rivers","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia AG asks SEC to take action against LSU's 'contempt for the rules'","description":"The Georgia Attorney General blasted LSU in a letter to SEC commissioner Greg Sankey, encouraging sanctions against the Tigers, \"up to and including expulsion.\"","published":"2026-11-19T04:59:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/50524054/georgia-ag-asks-sec-take-action-vs-lsu-expulsion","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach and Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama running back prospect AK Dear no longer with team","description":"Alabama tailback AK Dear, a former four-star prospect who was poised to make an impact before suffering an injury in the summer, is no longer on the team.","published":"2026-11-18T19:16:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50523034/alabama-running-back-prospect-ak-dear-no-longer-team","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge questions LSU's claims the SEC 'hallucinated' citations","description":"At a hearing Wednesday in the SEC's lawsuit against LSU, a federal judge pushed back on LSU attorneys for using the word \"hallucinated\" in filing.","published":"2026-11-18T22:40:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522883/judge-questions-lsu-claims-sec-hallucinated-citations","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-18T22:17:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5067875/zach-lutmer","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zach_Lutmer"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Zach Lutmer","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zach_Lutmer","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:24Z","intro":"Zach Lutmer (born November 5, 2004) is an American college football defensive back for the Iowa Hawkeyes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Lutmer attended Central Lyon High School in Rock Rapids, Iowa, where he played defensive back and quarterback. During his career he set school records for total yards, rushing yards and points scored. As a sophomore, Lutmer was the Class 2A Player of the Year after recording 1,194 passing yards, eight passing touchdowns, 1,609 rushing yards with 23 rushing touchdowns on offense and four interceptions, with two returned for a touchdown on defense. As a junior, he had 1,016 passing yards with eight touchdowns, 1,246 rushing yards with 22 touchdowns, and four interceptions with one returned for a touchdown. During his senior year he had 1,357 passing yards with 16 touchdowns, 1,562 rushing yards with 22 touchdowns and three interceptions. Lutmer committed to the University of Iowa to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Lutmer played in two games and redshirted his first year at Iowa in 2023. As a redshirt freshman in 2024, he played in all 13 games and had 14 tackles and one interception. Lutmer entered his redshirt sophomore year in 2025 as a starter."}]}}